# Additional Development Guidelines

The following sections should be added to the existing `.augment-guidelines` file to make it more comprehensive.

## Testing Guidelines
- Write tests for all new features and significant changes
- Use Vitest for unit and component testing
- Follow the AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert) for test structure
- Mock external dependencies and API calls
- Test components with Vue Test Utils, focusing on:
  - Component rendering and props validation
  - Event handling and emissions
  - Conditional rendering and state changes
- Aim for >80% test coverage for critical application paths
- Run tests before committing code: `yarn test`
- Write tests for error scenarios and edge cases

## Accessibility Standards
- Follow WCAG 2.1 AA compliance standards
- Ensure proper keyboard navigation for all interactive elements
- Maintain color contrast ratios of at least 4.5:1 for normal text
- Provide ARIA labels for all interactive elements without visible text
- Implement focus states for all interactive elements
- Test with screen readers periodically
- Use semantic HTML elements appropriately
- Ensure all form elements have associated labels
- Provide text alternatives for non-text content

## Git Workflow
- Branch naming: `feature/short-description`, `bugfix/issue-description`
- Commit messages: Use present tense with clear descriptions
- Create PRs with detailed descriptions of changes
- Require at least one code review before merging
- Squash commits when merging to maintain clean history
- Keep PRs focused on a single feature or fix
- Reference issue numbers in commit messages and PR descriptions
- Run tests locally before pushing code

## Error Handling Strategy
- Use try/catch blocks for async operations
- Implement consistent error feedback for users
- Log errors to console in development, consider a logging service in production
- Create reusable error components for common error scenarios
- Handle API errors with appropriate HTTP status codes
- Provide fallback UI for failed component loading
- Use error boundaries where appropriate
- Validate user input before submission

## Documentation Requirements
- Add JSDoc comments for all functions and composables
- Document component props with descriptions and types
- Keep README updated with new features and changes
- Document API endpoints with request/response examples
- Include usage examples for reusable components
- Document state management patterns and data flow
- Add comments for complex logic or algorithms
- Update documentation when changing existing functionality

## State Management Approach
- Use component-local state (`ref`, `reactive`) for UI-specific state
- Use composables for shared state between related components
- Consider Pinia for global application state
- Use `provide`/`inject` for prop drilling avoidance
- Keep state close to where it's used
- Implement state immutability patterns
- Document state management decisions
- Use `useState` for Nuxt-specific shared state

## Environment Configuration
- Store environment variables in `.env` files (not committed to git)
- Provide `.env.sample` files with required variables
- Use `runtimeConfig` in `nuxt.config.ts` for server-side variables
- Use `publicRuntimeConfig` for client-side variables
- Never expose API keys or secrets in client-side code
- Document all required environment variables
- Use different environment files for development/staging/production

## Performance Budgets
- Total bundle size: <250KB (compressed)
- First Contentful Paint: <1.8s on 4G connections
- Time to Interactive: <3.5s on 4G connections
- Largest Contentful Paint: <2.5s
- First Input Delay: <100ms
- Cumulative Layout Shift: <0.1
- Optimize images and use WebP format
- Implement code splitting for routes
- Lazy load off-screen components
- Monitor performance in production

## Deployment Strategy
- Use CI/CD pipeline for automated testing and deployment
- Implement staging environment for pre-production testing
- Use semantic versioning for releases
- Create release notes for significant updates
- Implement feature flags for gradual rollouts
- Have rollback plan for failed deployments
- Monitor application performance and errors post-deployment
- Perform database migrations safely

## Security Guidelines
- Implement Content Security Policy
- Sanitize all user inputs
- Use HTTPS for all connections
- Implement proper authentication and authorization
- Regularly update dependencies
- Follow OWASP security best practices
- Avoid exposing sensitive information in client-side code
- Use secure cookies with appropriate flags
